Unlike pleasure, knowledge compounds — each discovery builds on previous ones (Newton: 'standing on the shoulders of giants'), generating accelerating returns that pleasure does not produce.
Ignorance is not neutral — it enables exploitation, disease, oppression, and error; knowledge is the antidote that has historically freed people from each of these.
The countries with the highest investment in research and knowledge creation (US, Germany, South Korea, Japan) have the highest standards of living — the causal direction runs from knowledge to flourishing.
